# Line-ending policy for this repository's own checkout (distinct from
# sbak/templates/dot-gitattributes, which is the file generated INTO
# bootstrapped projects). Without this, a Windows clone with git's common
# core.autocrlf=true default checks every text file out as CRLF — and the
# kit's deterministic integrity check (golden-bootstrap --check-manifest)
# then reports a false STALE, because it hashes bytes that git rewrote on
# the way to disk. Force LF on disk for all tracked text so a clean clone
# verifies identically on Windows, macOS, and Linux. (ZIP arrival is
# unaffected — no git conversion touches ZIP bytes.)
* text=auto eol=lf
